//
// Returns .npmrc lines that authenticate npm to this server as the caller. A caller that sent its user name and password with Basic gets `_auth = <base64 of user:encrypted password>`, where the encrypted password is the value `GET /api/security/encryptedPassword` returns; the password itself is never returned. A caller that sent an access or reference token gets that same token back: as `_auth = <base64 of user:token>` when it sent the token as a Basic password, and as `_authToken = <token>` when it sent it as a Bearer token or in `X-JFrog-Art-Api`. No other line is sent. Needs an authenticated caller. Errors use the `{"errors":[{"status","message"}]}` envelope.
